line 5 type: bug SUB-1204 a literal widens to its base type where tsc keeps the literal type; also by-design spec §1.6 `a && b` is `falsy_part(a) | b` and `a || b` is `truthy_part(a) | b`, even when `a`'s truthiness is known
line 6, 10 type: by-design spec §1.6 an assignment that may not run installs no narrowing, so the variable keeps its declared type
line 9 type: bug SUB-1204 a literal widens to its base type where tsc keeps the literal type; also by-design spec §1.6 `&&` keeps `number` and `boolean` whole in its falsy part, where tsc narrows to `0` or `false`
